    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and both its tests pass along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field: **`SILVER`** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **`BRONZE`**.\n\nThe `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from `openapi.yml`, and the response is produced by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` (the same place `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipNumber` are derived), so I put the change in those two spots to match the existing pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` property (string enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and a `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` and a small single-responsibility `membershipTier(Owner)` default method that returns `SILVER` when the name is unique (`namesakeCount == 0`) and an email is present, else `BRONZE`. It sits alongside the existing derivation helpers rather than bloating any other method, and reuses the mapper's established `expression`-based approach. It also guards against a null owner and a null `namesakeCount`.",
